\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Convergence of the Monte Carlo rank estimation as the sample size $|\Theta |$ increases. Subfigures (a) through (d) illustrate that at lower sample sizes ($10^1 - 10^3$), the estimation exhibits high variance (noise). As $|\Theta |$ approaches $10^5$ and $10^6$ (f), the curve stabilizes, confirming that the memory optimizations allow for sample sizes large enough to produce deterministic-like accuracy.}}{25}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:3}{{3}{25}{Convergence of the Monte Carlo rank estimation as the sample size $|\Theta |$ increases. Subfigures (a) through (d) illustrate that at lower sample sizes ($10^1 - 10^3$),